The experimental Log MDCK cell line permeability efflux ratio (B-A/A-B) value of the following SMILES CN(CC1(CO)CCCC1)C(=O)CCN1CCCCC1=O is 1.3261939. What is the experimental Log MDCK cell line permeability efflux ratio (B-A/A-B) value of a closely related molecule CN(CC1(CO)CCC1)C(=O)CCN1CCCCC1=O.
The protocol of the experimental assay is as follows: The assay makes use of human MDR1 transfected MDCK cells (NIH cell line in-licensed from Absorption Systems, PA, USA). The compounds were tested at 1$~\mu$ M concentration prepared in transport buffer (Hank's balanced salt solution with HEPES). MDR1-MDCK cells were cultured for 7 days in 96-well transwell insert plates (Corning, NY, USA). Insert plates were washed before the assay, and TEER (transepithelial electric resistance) was measured. These plates were loaded with test compound solution of 85~$\mu$ L for A-B transport and 260~$\mu$ L for B-A transport in the respective donor compartment. The volumes of receiver buffer (transport buffer supplemented with 1\% BSA) in the respective receiver compartment were 250 and 75~$\mu$ L, respectively. Here, 10~$\mu$ L samples were taken from the donor compartment (T = 0 time point). Assay plates were incubated for 120 min. At 120 min (T = 120 time point), samples from the respective donor (10~$\mu$ L) and receiver (50~$\mu$ L) compartments were taken. After addition of 40~$\mu$ L of transport buffer with BSA to donor samples, a crash solution (acetonitrile with internal standard, 110~$\mu$ L) was added to all samples. After centrifugation, 50~$\mu$ L of supernatant was transferred to a separate plate and mixed with 50~$\mu$ L of water. Samples were analyzed using LC-MS/MS coupled with a high throughput injection system. Analyte/internal standard area ratios were used for apparent permeability (P\textsubscript{app}), efflux ratio, and mass recovery estimation based on the equations below:
\begin{align*}
P_{app} &= \frac{dC_r}{dt} \cdot \frac{V_r}{A \cdot C_E} \\
\text{Mass balance} &= 100 \times \frac{(V_r \cdot C_{r}^{\text{final}}) + (V_d \cdot C_{d}^{\text{final}}))}{V_d \cdot C_E}
\end{align*}

where $\frac{dC_r}{dt}$ is the cumulative concentration in the receiver compartment versus time in $\mu$M $s^{-1}$, $V_r$ the volume of the receiver compartment in cm$^3$, $V_d$ the volume of the donor compartment in cm$^3$, $A$ the area of the inset (0.143 cm$2$ for 96-well insert), $C_E$ the estimated experimental concentration (time = 0) of the dosing solution, $C_r^{\text{final}}$ the concentration of the receiver at the end of the incubation period, and $C_d^{\text{final}}$ the concentration of the donor at the end of the incubation period.

Place the final answer at the end of your response in the format: **Answer: floating_point_number**. The final result should be a single floating point number.

